{"author":{"id":"aa05e8c12e0d734c8a7a4c8d0aa648556351b86541dd4c3132d1e0042d98b8af"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1790114688,"nonce":"mOWt2YdGw0Aq5IU20qJ3Tiw6qgU=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"UCE_lAHOULtcMc8AAAABSo3lis7zcI82","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"f188884c66f2e23fdb61d59a2756b4ffe27a6b06cf05e7ae8a7e1820f302fcd5"},"target":"cb41b668ac34de7668be0421cb39f5d44afee49432c92854d82cc2ecced4085e","message":"# Original specs\n\nOne table to edit, with sortable columns, that contains data about servers, storage bays, network devices and spare parts; these different IT elements do not need the exact same columns, but we will not make any constraints/checks. \nDifferentiate content columns used for computations (two columns: “Quantity” and “Impact manufacturing + distribution + EOL”) and for final report (all columns). \n\nThe table has a lot of columns, so we are proposing three editing/reporting modes: \n- Simple/elementary, only the mandatory fields are displayed and filled. \n- Normal/regular, the mandatory and recommended fields are displayed and filled. \n- Advanced/extensive: all fields are displayed and filled. \nWe have to discuss about what happens when switching editing mode.  \n\nTable with the following columns:\n- [x] Category: editable drop-down list, mandatory\n  - [x] Pre-populate with: server, compute server, storage bay, network device, spare part\n- [x] Name: text, mandatory\n- [x] Rack unit: number\n- [x] Quantity: number, mandatory\n- [x] Description: text, recommended\n- [x] Datacenter: drop down list (from Scope), mandatory\n- [x] Reused HW / repurposed / second hand HW: checkbox, mandatory\n  - [x] Logic: If yes, the embodied emissions are not considered in the computation\n- [x] Impact manufacturing: number, recommended\n- [x] Impact manufacturing + distribution + EOL: number, mandatory\n- [x] ResilioDB hash: text, recommended\n- [x] CPU – name: text, recommended\n- [x] CPU – quantity: number, mandatory\n- [x] CPU – lithography: number\n- [x] CPU - die size: number\n- [x] CPU – cores: number\n- [x] Memory – quantity: number, mandatory\n- [x] Memory – size: number, mandatory\n- [x] Memory – total: number, calculated from the two previous columns (quantity * size)\n- [x] Storage type: drop down list (HDD, SSD)\n- [x] Storage – quantity: number, mandatory\n- [x] Storage - size: number, mandatory\n- [x] Storage - total: number, calculated from the two previous columns (quantity * size)\n- [x] Storage technology: drop down list (SLC, MLC, TLC, QLC)\n- [x] Storage casing: drop down list (M2, 2.5 inch)\n- [x] GPU – name: text, recommended\n- [x] GPU – quantity: number, mandatory\n- [x] GPU – lithography: number\n- [x] GPU – die size: number\n- [x] GPU – memory: number, recommended\n- [x] Network – quantity ports: number, recommended\n- [x] PSU – quantity: number\n- [x] PSU – power: number\n\n# Questions\n\n- [ ] Category: \"editable drop-down list, mandatory\"\n  - [ ] does that mean that the user should also be able to input arbitrary text in this one ?","files":null}]}